@startuml c2_agent_failure_routing
title C2 -- agent-failure routing through CallbackRouter

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2

actor "community agent" as Agent
participant "POST /jobs/{id}/agent-failure\n(api/routers/jobs.py)" as API
participant "CallbackRouter\n(callbacks/router.py)" as CR
participant "FailureHandler\n(callbacks/failure_handler.py)" as FH
participant "RenderOrchestrator" as RO
participant "RenderLifecycle\n.handle_chunk_failed" as LC

Agent -> API : POST agent-failure(job_id, error)

note over API #ffe5e5
  BEFORE C2 (current):
  agent_failure() calls
  RenderOrchestrator.on_job_failed
  DIRECTLY. Skips CallbackRouter
  and its is_job_terminal guard.
end note

note over API #ddffdd
  AFTER C2:
  agent_failure() calls
  callback_router.route(
      job_id, FAILURE, error)
  Same path Vast/Modal monitors
  already use via _on_failure.
end note

API -[#009900,bold]-> CR : route(job_id, FAILURE, error)
CR -> CR : is_job_terminal(job_id)?

alt job already terminal (idempotent skip)
    CR -[#888888]-> API : log + return
    API -[#888888]-> Agent : 200 (no-op)
    note right of CR
      Filters double-fire from
      retried HTTP calls or
      future failure sources.
      Same guard Vast/Modal
      already get.
    end note
else job still active
    CR -> FH : handle(job_id, error)
    FH -> RO : on_job_failed(job_id, error)
    RO -> LC : handle_chunk_failed(job_id, error)
    LC -> LC : retry decision\nmark_failed\ndrain queue\nreconcile group
    LC --> RO : ok
    RO --> FH : ok
    FH --> CR : ok
    CR --> API : ok
    API --> Agent : 200
end

legend right
  Files touched (3 files, ~10 lines)
  ----
  serverV2/bootstrap.py
    Container.__init__ adds callback_router field;
    build_container stores the router on the container
    (currently constructed but not exposed).

  serverV2/main.py
    jobs.init(c.job_service,
             orchestrator=c.orchestrator,
             callback_router=c.callback_router)

  serverV2/api/routers/jobs.py
    init() accepts callback_router; stores in
    module-level _callback_router.
    agent_failure body becomes:
      _get_callback_router().route(
        job_id=job_id,
        outcome=CallbackOutcome.FAILURE,
        error=error,
      )
end legend

@enduml
